# width: 120
# height: 40
# A TITLED context menu is `rows + 2` tall, the same as a dropdown. The
# title is painted INSIDE the top border by `overlay.frameLook`, so the
# height that also reserved a row for it left one empty line above the
# bottom border of every right-click menu in the app. The reference
# editor (`src/ui/context_menu.rs`) has the same off-by-one; this
# departs from it (`docs/PARITY.md`).
write a.txt hello
open a.txt
rightclick 50 2
expect screen contains "Save"
expect screen lacks "│                           │"
